# What a target can't draw yet of what the gallery uses: the target, then the
# element as compiler/language/targets.hpp names it, a line each. The gallery's test
# fails while this differs from what's so, so it only ever gets shorter; a new
# target starts with everything here and is done when none of its lines are left.
# A terminal draws no pictures, so it can't show one alone, on a card or a table's
# row, crop one in place, match a collage's colors, or copy, save or keep a picture of
# a collage, nor save or copy one as SVG yet, and it has no screen of its own to take a screenshot of, nor pictures to
# choose from files, a calendar's rows are moved by its commands, not dragged, and what's
# said as a row's time comes is the bell and its words, without buttons. A paper is
# written on in place, which a terminal doesn't do yet, and a collage's layer is drawn
# or reshaped by a pointer's drag, or picked as a group, or zoomed, which a terminal has none of; nor does it pick colors yet.
